WEBVTT

NOTE Captions from NASA (images.nasa.gov, jsc2025m000002), converted from SRT.

1
00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.769
>> Imagine exercising in space,

2
00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.737
something astronauts on

3
00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.138
the International Space Station

4
00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.039
do for a couple hours

5
00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.474
almost every day.

6
00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.575
There's little gravity,

7
00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.509
so you'd need to be strapped

8
00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.710
to your treadmill with a harness

9
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.011
so you wouldn't float away.

10
00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.046
There's limited space,

11
00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:13.680
but that's fine

12
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.514
since your treadmill

13
00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.782
could be attached to the ceiling

14
00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.716
or a wall.

15
00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.118
Every surface is a usable one

16
00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.452
when in microgravity.

17
00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.353
To keep your bones strong

18
00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:20.854
and safeguard

19
00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.955
your muscles and heart,

20
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.655
you'd really need to stick

21
00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.257
to your exercise regiment,

22
00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.191
involving three pieces

23
00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.860
of exercise equipment.

24
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.827
The station's treadmill

25
00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.462
is like what you'd use on Earth,

26
00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.463
but it's got a specialized

27
00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.198
vibration isolation system

28
00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:32.699
to make sure that

29
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.600
the force of your feet

30
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.434
striking the treadmill

31
00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.402
won't shake the station's

32
00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.603
research experiments

33
00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.638
or even move the entire station.

34
00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.939
The station's spin class style

35
00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.141
exercise bike has similar

36
00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.909
vibration isolation.

37
00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.910
Finally, there's a machine

38
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.911
which allows astronauts

39
00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.779
to mimic weight lifting

40
00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:46.913
in low gravity.

41
00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:47.914
It uses cylinders of air

42
00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.315
to provide resistance.

43
00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.216
Squats, deadlifts,

44
00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.384
bench presses, and more

45
00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:51.985
are all part of

46
00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.720
that space workout mix.

47
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.421
Instead of multiple

48
00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.455
workout machines,

49
00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.222
on future trips

50
00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.424
to the moon and Mars,

51
00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.758
astronauts will likely use

52
00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.460
a single rowing device.

53
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.661
Spacecraft will be more compact

54
00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.762
than the space station

55
00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.663
and rowing movements,

56
00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.898
especially with the resistance

57
00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.132
turned up, will offer

58
00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.133
a full body workout,

59
00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:07.801
even allowing for

60
00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.769
weight lifting-like exercises.

61
00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.237
For astronauts, weight lifting,

62
00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:11.671
no matter what

63
00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.739
equipment you use,

64
00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:13.606
is needed to maintain

65
00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.375
the body's capabilities.

66
00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.709
So say you weigh 150 pounds

67
00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:17.710
on Earth.

68
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.378
In space, you'd want

69
00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.012
to be able to squat

70
00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.613
at least that same weight.

71
00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.281
Why? To maintain

72
00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.749
the muscle strength you need

73
00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.716
to carry yourself around

74
00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.884
when you come home.

75
00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.819
And really, what's a better

76
00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.787
workout motivator than that?
